findings.body:
After this PR, `evt.destinationCalendar` can be either a non-empty array (when the event type or the organizer user has a destination calendar) or `null`. The collective branch is:

```ts
if (isTeamEventType && eventType.schedulingType === "COLLECTIVE") {
  evt.destinationCalendar?.push(...teamDestinationCalendars);
}
```

If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `null`, the optional-chained `push` is a no-op. That is exactly the scenario this PR is supposed to support: a COLLECTIVE event whose organizer user has not configured a destination calendar but whose team members have. `teamDestinationCalendars` is collected correctly, but it never reaches `event.destinationCalendar`, so `EventManager.createAllCalendarEvents` falls back to "first connected calendar" and the team hosts are not invited to their calendars. Initialize `destinationCalendar` as `[]` (or fallback to `[]` instead of `null`) and `push` unconditionally.

The fallback line is:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
```

If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `[]` (e.g. for a collective COLLECTIVE booking whose organizer has no destination calendar - the same scenario where the bug above drops the team destinations), then `mainHostDestinationCalendar` is `undefined` and `.integration` throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined`. Guard with optional chaining or treat the empty case as "not google_calendar" (current desired behavior is to fall back to Cal Video).
